thag1.33:1.1 starts: Just as one would be good
thag1.33:1.2 starts: to one’s dear only child,
thag1.33:1.3 starts: one should be good to all creatures
thag1.33:1.4 starts: everywhere.
thag1.1:4.1 starts: My hut is roofed, comfortable,
thag1.1:4.2 starts: my mind, well-centered,
thag1.1:4.3 starts: I remain ardent.
thag1.1:4.4 starts: So, rain-deva.
thag1.16:1.1 starts: Just as a fine thoroughbred steed,
thag1.16:1.2 starts: with swishing tail & mane
thag1.16:1.3 starts: runs with next-to-no effort,
thag1.16:1.4 starts: so my days & nights
thag1.16:1.5 starts: run with next-to-no effort
thag1.16:1.6 starts: now that I’ve gained a pleasure
thag1.23:1.1 starts: I—having eaten honey-rice
thag1.23:1.2 starts: in a bamboo patch
thag1.23:1.3 starts: and rightly grasping
thag1.23:1.4 starts: the aggregates’
thag1.23:1.5 starts: will return to the hillside,
thag1.23:1.6 starts: intent
thag1.25:1.1 starts: Like splendor, his mind,
thag1.25:1.2 starts: continually fruitful:
thag1.25:1.3 starts: Attack a monk like that,
thag1.25:1.4 starts: you Dark One,
thag1.29:1.1 starts: Hārita,
thag1.29:1.2 starts: and, straightening your mind
thag1.29:1.3 starts: —like a fletcher, an arrow—
thag1.29:1.4 starts: shatter ignorance
thag1.31:1.1 starts: Touched by gnats & mosquitoes,
thag1.31:1.2 starts: in the wilds, the great forest,
thag1.31:1.3 starts: like a nāga elephant
thag1.31:1.4 starts: mindful,
thag1.43:1.1 starts: So freed! So freed!
thag1.43:1.2 starts: So thoroughly freed am I
thag1.43:1.3 starts: from three crooked things:
thag1.43:1.4 starts: my sickles, my shovels, my plows.
thag1.43:1.5 starts: Even if they were here,
thag1.43:1.6 starts: I’d be done with them,
thag1.43:1.7 starts: Do jhāna, Sumaṅgala.
thag1.43:1.8 starts: Sumaṅgala, stay heedful.
